            <ArticleTitle>Unrecognized stent embolization causing recurrent chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E74-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Numerous methods have been described for retrieving or addressing stents that have embolized in the coronary arteries. Almost all of these prior reports address the &quot;freshly&quot; embolized stent with retrieval or deployment occurring during the same index procedure during which the embolization occurred. We describe a case of a thrombosed, chronically embolized coronary stent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
